  "query_preview": "..\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nHigh pressure will continue to deliver fair weather for NE Montana\nwith high to mid clouds at times through tonight and Thursday as\nwell as light area winds. For Thursday night into the weekend, a\nfrontal passage will deliver gusty northwest winds at times as\nwell as cooler temperatures. Consideration of a Lake Wind Advisory\nfor Fort Peck Lake may at some point be appropriate. Ensembles \ncontinue to keep significant rain and snow chances to the \nsouthwest of our CWA or across southern and central MT during this\nperiod.\n\nEnsembles show the lingering trough sliding into the central U.S.\nlate in the weekend, and NE Montana on the leading edge of a \nflattening ridge situated over the western CONUS. This results in\ncool temperatures but dry weather.\n\nThe next precipitation event may come Monday or Monday night with\nthe next disturbance moving in from the Pacific NW.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & NBM DEVIATIONS:\n\nNBM held the line this cycle with little deviation necessary aside\nfrom consistency and collaboration. Confidence remains high on\nmild and dry conditions over the next couple of days with colder\ntemperatures settling in for the late weekend into early next week\ntime frame. TFJ",
